Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.14),
 gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-mpv, libmpv2 | libmpv1, libegl1
Description: small video player for GNOME, built on mpv
 Nausicaa plays your videos, and nothing else. It is a simple window around
 the mpv engine, with the mouse habits of VLC:
  - click on the picture to pause, double-click for full screen (without
    pausing), mouse wheel for the volume with an on-screen display;
  - pause when the window is minimised, resume when it comes back;
  - resume each video where you left it;
  - open one episode and the following ones are queued, in natural order;
  - play queue with shuffle, repeat, drag to reorder, saved as a playlist
    (.m3u, .m3u8, .xspf, .pls are read);
  - audio tracks, subtitles (files next to the video are found), speed,
    frame by frame, picture capture.
 It follows the desktop theme (Adwaita, light/dark, accent colour).
